st of the hero is that he also  has a wolf form just like the hero of  Twilight does and his song selection for  the howling stone segments are nearly  all songs from Ocarina of Time or  Majora's Mask both of which are  Adventures of the hero of time  furthermore we know that the shade is an  ancestor to at least the hero of  Twilight because of the in-game piece of  dialogue where he mentions the hero of  Twilight is carrying the hero's  bloodline and he's hell bound on  teaching his secrets to the next  generation the hero of Twilight after  he's done teaching the hero of Twilight  all of his super secret samurai sword  skills he states that he has at last  eased his regrets before uttering his  final farewell but once we begin looking  at the visual clues we can get from the  shades appearance questions begin to  start popping up most obviously the hero  shade is fully clad in armor now while  this could be personal armor he had  whipped up for himself later on in life  I tend to think that it's Knightly armor  if you look closely at the more raggedy  portions you can see the armor included  a layer of chain mail which has been  either pierced or rotted away and  chainmail is not only a historical  staple of Knightly armor but is worn by  all the Hylian soldiers in Twilight  Princess the helmet is also rather showy  which was typical in historical times as  a show of rank for example Roman  centurions who outranked regular  soldiers would wear these really floofy  things on their heads as a sign of their  rank and authority you don't see any  personal armor sets looking that showy  throughout history unless of course  we're talking about Skyrim his armor  does have markings on it but no matter  how much  I can't link the designs to any people  group across the zelda franchise if you  think you know something about the  markings on his armor please feel free  to let me know in the comments below now  let's look at the state of his overall  of self the fact that th